From b11955cf639deebce2200a5d3546308e70edece9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 11:08:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(auth): bind deletion fence to the row read
 snapshot

Take row ownership and token-generation bases from the same picker-scoped store read, preventing peer deletions during seeding from becoming additions. Root update-only persistence returns unavailable rather than empty membership for corrupt or missing pool stores, preserving runtime credentials until a valid root read.

Proof: all four new cases fail on de49489fe3 (corrupt/missing root, deletion during load, picker parse count); 1263 auth/pool tests pass across 126 files, 3 skipped; scripts/check all 21 checks pass.
